[ti:A Heart Full of Light]
[ar:for Shayan]

[00:02.00]there are people the world grows softer for holding
[00:09.00]and you have always been one of them
[00:16.00]kindness arrives in a room a breath before you do
[00:23.00]and stays long after you have gone
[00:30.00]you stayed gentle on days that would harden anyone
[00:37.00]you stayed kind while your own body grew tired
[00:44.00]i have watched you carry more than most could lift
[00:51.00]and still choose tenderness over bitterness
[00:58.00]so let this be a letter written in light
[01:05.00]for a heart as rare as yours
[01:12.00]when the night feels a little too loud
[01:19.00]i want you to really hear this
[01:26.00]you are not alone, not now, not ever
[01:33.00]even when i am not beside you
[01:40.00]i am hoping for you, holding you in every prayer
[01:47.00]so breathe, i have got you
[01:54.00]some people will never understand what they see
[02:01.00]they miss the whole universe inside you
[02:08.00]do not let small words shrink your big heart
[02:15.00]the ones who mock have never had to be this brave
[02:22.00]you are kinder than they will ever be
[02:29.00]and that has always been your quiet beauty
[02:36.00]i know you are tired
[02:43.00]the deep kind that sleep cannot fix
[02:50.00]you are allowed to rest, to fall apart
[02:57.00]in front of someone who thinks no less of you
[03:04.00]rest, my friend, the world can wait
[03:11.00]you have carried it long enough
[03:18.00]on the days you cannot find a reason to smile
[03:25.00]borrow mine
[03:32.00]you are not your illness
[03:39.00]not what the mirror shows on a hard morning
[03:46.00]you are the warmth people feel around you
[03:53.00]the laugh that makes a room lighter
[04:00.00]the friend who shows up when it costs him everything
[04:07.00]if i could give you my health i would
[04:14.00]without a single second thought
[04:21.00]since i cannot, i will give you this
[04:28.00]every ounce of love i have, for as long as i have it
[04:35.00]you are worth all of it, and so much more
[04:42.00]so if the night ever feels too long
[04:49.00]come back here and remember who you are
[04:56.00]you are treasured beyond measure
[05:03.00]keep shining, gentle one
[05:10.00]the world is brighter for having you in it
